\name{sdrf_samples}
\alias{sdrf_samples}
\title{Each sample's characteristics and factor values, merged over its rows, ages parsed}
\usage{
sdrf_samples(path, timeout = 60)
}
\arguments{
\item{path}{Path to a \code{.sdrf.tsv} file.}

\item{timeout}{Seconds to allow, or \code{NULL} to wait indefinitely.
}

}
\description{
One row per sample, column and position: what each source name's rows agree on, the columns they disagree about named and withheld, and characteristics[age] read into years.

Calls mzLib's \code{SdrfSampleBlock.BySourceName}: the sample half of the document - \code{source name},
every \code{characteristics[...]}, every \code{factor value[...]} - per sample, merged over the sample's
rows. A sample is a \code{source name}, matched ignoring case and surrounding space, so one sample
measured in three fractions is one sample. Where its rows \strong{disagree} - one fraction says
\code{normal} and another \code{COVID-19} - mzLib names the column and withholds it rather than let the
first row win.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_sdrf_samples}: \code{path}, \code{sample_count} samples (distinct source names),
  \code{row_count} data rows, \code{conflict_count} (sample x column pairs withheld as conflicting),
  \code{problems} (rows mzLib could not place; empty for a well-formed document), \code{caveats},
  \code{column_names}, and \code{records}, a long data.frame with one row per sample x column x position,
  samples in document order: \code{source_name}; \code{sample_row_count}, the rows carrying the sample;
  \code{column_name}, as the header spells it; \code{column_kind} (\code{source_name}, \code{characteristic} or
  \code{factor_value}); \code{position} (1 for the first occurrence of a repeated column; \code{NA} on a
  conflicting row); \code{status} (\code{"agreed"} or \code{"conflicting"}); and \code{value}, the cell verbatim,
  \code{NA} when conflicting.

  On the rows for the age characteristic six more columns hold the parsed age, with the meanings
  \code{\link{sdrf_parse_ages}} gives: \code{age_years}, \code{age_min_years} and \code{age_max_years} in years,
  \code{age_precision}, \code{age_follows_specification} and \code{age_refusal}. On every other row they are
  \code{NA}.

}
\section{Key samples within a document}{


A source name is unique only within one document - two studies may both have a \code{"Sample 1"} -
so across documents key a sample on the document as well.

}
